    "name": "Method/Flaw/Argument Part Answer Choice Translation Spreadsheet",
    "text": "3\nMethod/Flaw/Argument Part Answer Choice Translation Spreadsheet\nInstructions\n\nMake a spreadsheet with three columns, or use this template:\n\nColumn 1: Vexing Answer Choice\n\nColumn 2: Answer Choice Translation\n\nColumn 3: Corresponding Stimulus\n\nCollect all the difficult answer choices to translate, focusing especially on Method/Flaw/Argument Part answer choices.\n\nThis could include harvesting answer choices from your sections immediately after you're done or going back over old sections to harvest answer choices.\n\nWrite the difficult answers in the Vexing Answer Choice column of the spreadsheet, one answer choice per row.\n\nTranslate the answers in the Answer Choice Translation column of the spreadsheet.\n\nIn the Corresponding Stimulus column of the spreadsheet, write an example stimulus which would make the answer choice in that row correct.\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
